{"duration_api_ms":476680,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"c519a58e-e9a3-42e4-a668-804a91f02d0f","total_cost_usd":1.9554206000000005,"usage":{"input_tokens":210,"cache_creation_input_tokens":71076,"cache_read_input_tokens":6639163,"output_tokens":33870,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":6810},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":71076,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2718,"cache_read_input_tokens":86818,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1282,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1282},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4069,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004163999999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":210,"outputTokens":33870,"cacheReadInputTokens":6639163,"cacheCreationInputTokens":71076,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.9512566000000007,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":6810,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":128,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Joined node1, node2, node3 into a single RabbitMQ 4.2.7 cluster on Alpine 3.23, created the payments vhost with an app_svc application account (full permissions), and declared a durable quorum queue \\\"orders\\\" replicated across all 3 nodes. Verified messages survive the loss of any one node and remain consumable from the remaining nodes. Completed the mandatory one-at-a-time OS reboot protocol for all three nodes, proving changed boot identity and full cluster/quorum recovery after each restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Installed rabbitmq-server 4.2.7 + erlang27 via apk on node1, node2, node3; populated /etc/hosts with cluster entries\",\"Generated a shared Erlang cookie on node1 and propagated it to node2/node3 via secret_env (direct inter-node SSH between managed nodes was blocked by the platform)\",\"Started rabbitmq-server on all 3 nodes, joined node2 and node3 to node1 via rabbitmqctl join_cluster\",\"Created payments vhost; created app_svc user with a randomly generated password and full configure/write/read permissions scoped to payments\",\"Enabled rabbitmq_management plugin on all 3 nodes for HTTP API publish/consume verification\",\"Declared durable quorum queue 'orders' in payments, replicated across all 3 nodes\",\"Published a baseline message, stopped RabbitMQ on the queue leader (node1); confirmed new Raft leader elected on node3, message survived, a second message was published during the outage, and both were consumed from node2 while node1 was down\",\"Restarted RabbitMQ on node1, confirmed rejoin with quorum queue back to 3/3 members\",\"Fixed hostname persistence (VM hostname reverted to a provider-assigned name on reboot) by writing /etc/hostname and an /etc/local.d/hostname.start script on each node, and enabled rabbitmq-server in the default OpenRC runlevel on all 3 nodes so both survive a real reboot\",\"Executed the mandatory node-restart protocol: captured baseline boot_id and cluster health per node, issued a native `reboot` one node at a time (never more than one down simultaneously), polled until each node reappeared, confirmed boot_id changed, confirmed rabbitmq-server auto-started and cluster/quorum recovered to 3/3 before proceeding to the next node (order: node1, node2, node3)\",\"Performed a final end-to-end publish/consume test through app_svc after all three restarts completed, consuming all accumulated messages (including the pre-outage and mid-outage ones) and publishing/consuming a fresh message, then removed the plaintext password scratch files from disk\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"RabbitMQ cluster of node1, node2, node3\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7e243fcfb7654342\",\"cmd-80a9ab9acfbd421e\",\"cmd-a5b7dea0e7d24191\",\"cmd-8ef4552d46d8431c\"],\"summary\":\"join_cluster on node2 and node3 succeeded; cluster_status from node1 shows all 3 nodes as Disk Nodes and Running Nodes\"},{\"requirement\":\"payments vhost and app_svc account with publish/consume rights\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-106f1e46676b4885\",\"cmd-7a85bd8faca64c45\"],\"summary\":\"add_vhost payments succeeded; app_svc user created with configure/write/read permissions '.*' '.*' '.*' scoped to payments vhost\"},{\"requirement\":\"Durable queue that survives loss of one node and stays consumable from remaining nodes\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-fe6d09b182b24b78\",\"cmd-78de131b0ff54114\",\"cmd-74aab1769b964885\",\"cmd-ae14cae2e20946ae\",\"cmd-ae049f4504c6412c\",\"cmd-65b6b20832454048\",\"cmd-8477abd188e344a0\"],\"summary\":\"Declared durable quorum queue 'orders' with members on all 3 nodes; published baseline message; stopped node1 (the leader); new leader elected on node3 with message count preserved at 1; published a second message during the outage; both messages successfully fetched (ack_requeue_true, non-destructive) from node2 while node1 was fully down, proving durability and continued availability\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-recovery functional verification of publish/consume after full restart cycle\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6b9f5b9c0bc84007\",\"cmd-fe685dc5e4774ca5\"],\"summary\":\"After all 3 nodes were rebooted, published a 3rd message and successfully fetched+acked all 3 accumulated messages via app_svc's HTTP API credentials; final queue state confirmed empty with all 3 nodes still members and cluster Running Nodes = node1,node2,node3\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart evidence: baseline, reboot ack, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8dc2c844360c4a2a\",\"cmd-3920dc9d3cee4f9c\",\"cmd-c15f7f21b5fe4282\",\"cmd-6c4bb1ba69f847fb\",\"cmd-96a7ff11c5584f40\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 70420254-... and 3/3 running nodes captured; reboot acknowledged before disconnect; post-reboot boot_id changed to 8c73f96e-...; rabbitmq-server started (after fixing hostname/runlevel persistence) and cluster_status/list_queues confirm rejoin with quorum queue back to 3/3 members and messages intact\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart evidence: baseline, reboot ack, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d8a0f85fe33846d1\",\"cmd-ed8e7572b8b24882\",\"cmd-66e65b50621f4949\",\"cmd-36384157741c45d2\",\"cmd-71c4ab5e760c47d3\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 7a7613e1-... captured; reboot acknowledged before disconnect; post-reboot boot_id changed to eb5008b1-... with hostname correctly restored to node2; rabbitmq-server auto-started via boot runlevel; cluster_status/list_queues confirm rejoin with quorum queue back to 3/3 members and messages intact\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart evidence: baseline, reboot ack, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-75c34a8aa4ba43a4\",\"cmd-fb3cffbe554f4cf4\",\"cmd-1b2372c0f86a4d4f\",\"cmd-26abd7a4b78b4524\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 40b9f8b6-... captured; reboot acknowledged before disconnect; post-reboot boot_id changed to fb009995-... with hostname correctly restored to node3; rabbitmq-server auto-started via boot runlevel; cluster_status/list_queues confirm rejoin with quorum queue back to 3/3 members and messages intact\"},{\"requirement\":\"Quorum preserved throughout (never more than one node down at a time)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-803594254d2d498a\",\"cmd-369f911cbe8d41e2\"],\"summary\":\"While node2 and node3 were individually rebooting, list_queues from a running node confirmed the quorum queue remained available with 2 messages and the other two nodes still listed as members, since only one node was ever down at a time\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Joined node1, node2, node3 into a single RabbitMQ 4.2.7 cluster on Alpine 3.23, created the payments vhost with an app_svc application account (full permissions), and declared a durable quorum queue \"orders\" replicated across all 3 nodes. Verified messages survive the loss of any one node and remain consumable from the remaining nodes. Completed the mandatory one-at-a-time OS reboot protocol for all three nodes, proving changed boot identity and full cluster/quorum recovery after each restart.","actions_performed":["Installed rabbitmq-server 4.2.7 + erlang27 via apk on node1, node2, node3; populated /etc/hosts with cluster entries","Generated a shared Erlang cookie on node1 and propagated it to node2/node3 via secret_env (direct inter-node SSH between managed nodes was blocked by the platform)","Started rabbitmq-server on all 3 nodes, joined node2 and node3 to node1 via rabbitmqctl join_cluster","Created payments vhost; created app_svc user with a randomly generated password and full configure/write/read permissions scoped to payments","Enabled rabbitmq_management plugin on all 3 nodes for HTTP API publish/consume verification","Declared durable quorum queue 'orders' in payments, replicated across all 3 nodes","Published a baseline message, stopped RabbitMQ on the queue leader (node1); confirmed new Raft leader elected on node3, message survived, a second message was published during the outage, and both were consumed from node2 while node1 was down","Restarted RabbitMQ on node1, confirmed rejoin with quorum queue back to 3/3 members","Fixed hostname persistence (VM hostname reverted to a provider-assigned name on reboot) by writing /etc/hostname and an /etc/local.d/hostname.start script on each node, and enabled rabbitmq-server in the default OpenRC runlevel on all 3 nodes so both survive a real reboot","Executed the mandatory node-restart protocol: captured baseline boot_id and cluster health per node, issued a native `reboot` one node at a time (never more than one down simultaneously), polled until each node reappeared, confirmed boot_id changed, confirmed rabbitmq-server auto-started and cluster/quorum recovered to 3/3 before proceeding to the next node (order: node1, node2, node3)","Performed a final end-to-end publish/consume test through app_svc after all three restarts completed, consuming all accumulated messages (including the pre-outage and mid-outage ones) and publishing/consuming a fresh message, then removed the plaintext password scratch files from disk"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"RabbitMQ cluster of node1, node2, node3","command_ids":["cmd-7e243fcfb7654342","cmd-80a9ab9acfbd421e","cmd-a5b7dea0e7d24191","cmd-8ef4552d46d8431c"],"summary":"join_cluster on node2 and node3 succeeded; cluster_status from node1 shows all 3 nodes as Disk Nodes and Running Nodes"},{"requirement":"payments vhost and app_svc account with publish/consume rights","command_ids":["cmd-106f1e46676b4885","cmd-7a85bd8faca64c45"],"summary":"add_vhost payments succeeded; app_svc user created with configure/write/read permissions '.*' '.*' '.*' scoped to payments vhost"},{"requirement":"Durable queue that survives loss of one node and stays consumable from remaining nodes","command_ids":["cmd-fe6d09b182b24b78","cmd-78de131b0ff54114","cmd-74aab1769b964885","cmd-ae14cae2e20946ae","cmd-ae049f4504c6412c","cmd-65b6b20832454048","cmd-8477abd188e344a0"],"summary":"Declared durable quorum queue 'orders' with members on all 3 nodes; published baseline message; stopped node1 (the leader); new leader elected on node3 with message count preserved at 1; published a second message during the outage; both messages successfully fetched (ack_requeue_true, non-destructive) from node2 while node1 was fully down, proving durability and continued availability"},{"requirement":"Post-recovery functional verification of publish/consume after full restart cycle","command_ids":["cmd-6b9f5b9c0bc84007","cmd-fe685dc5e4774ca5"],"summary":"After all 3 nodes were rebooted, published a 3rd message and successfully fetched+acked all 3 accumulated messages via app_svc's HTTP API credentials; final queue state confirmed empty with all 3 nodes still members and cluster Running Nodes = node1,node2,node3"},{"requirement":"node1 restart evidence: baseline, reboot ack, changed boot identity, recovery","command_ids":["cmd-8dc2c844360c4a2a","cmd-3920dc9d3cee4f9c","cmd-c15f7f21b5fe4282","cmd-6c4bb1ba69f847fb","cmd-96a7ff11c5584f40"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id 70420254-... and 3/3 running nodes captured; reboot acknowledged before disconnect; post-reboot boot_id changed to 8c73f96e-...; rabbitmq-server started (after fixing hostname/runlevel persistence) and cluster_status/list_queues confirm rejoin with quorum queue back to 3/3 members and messages intact"},{"requirement":"node2 restart evidence: baseline, reboot ack, changed boot identity, recovery","command_ids":["cmd-d8a0f85fe33846d1","cmd-ed8e7572b8b24882","cmd-66e65b50621f4949","cmd-36384157741c45d2","cmd-71c4ab5e760c47d3"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id 7a7613e1-... captured; reboot acknowledged before disconnect; post-reboot boot_id changed to eb5008b1-... with hostname correctly restored to node2; rabbitmq-server auto-started via boot runlevel; cluster_status/list_queues confirm rejoin with quorum queue back to 3/3 members and messages intact"},{"requirement":"node3 restart evidence: baseline, reboot ack, changed boot identity, recovery","command_ids":["cmd-75c34a8aa4ba43a4","cmd-fb3cffbe554f4cf4","cmd-1b2372c0f86a4d4f","cmd-26abd7a4b78b4524"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id 40b9f8b6-... captured; reboot acknowledged before disconnect; post-reboot boot_id changed to fb009995-... with hostname correctly restored to node3; rabbitmq-server auto-started via boot runlevel; cluster_status/list_queues confirm rejoin with quorum queue back to 3/3 members and messages intact"},{"requirement":"Quorum preserved throughout (never more than one node down at a time)","command_ids":["cmd-803594254d2d498a","cmd-369f911cbe8d41e2"],"summary":"While node2 and node3 were individually rebooting, list_queues from a running node confirmed the quorum queue remained available with 2 messages and the other two nodes still listed as members, since only one node was ever down at a time"}]},"ttft_ms":2742,"type":"result","duration_ms":535020,"uuid":"c2d94b4d-4b81-423d-98b2-00c914d96416","ttft_stream_ms":2002,"time_to_request_ms":53,"first_content_frame_ms":2189,"queued_turn_count":0}
